<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Samuel Kirkland</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1741">1741</a>–<a href="/years/1808">1808</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Samuel Kirkland was an American Presbyterian missionary to the Oneida and other Iroquois nations. From 1766 he lived among the Oneida, converting many and helping keep them on the American side in the Revolutionary War. In 1793 he founded the Hamilton-Oneida Academy, which became Hamilton College.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/samuel-kirkland.jpg" alt="Samuel Kirkland" width="320" height="393" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Samuel_Kirkland_by_Augustus_Rockwell_detail.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
